{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run1:inflation:fermi","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:983831152a8626bf8fc59804831deb6247c70fc2510ac7515dfd053f34a87ff8","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"binary","positiveOutcomeId":"yes","probability":0.25},"questionHash":"sha256:cfe468fa9439bedeee3804a35583667745f13831322e2c91a89c02a1b211413b","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq5","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"CONJUNCT A (MOVE 10-yr average >= 105, 2027-2036). The decisive arithmetic is that MOVE is basis-point-normalized, so its level scales with the yield level: at a 4.0-4.5% 10y nominal the vol-neutral MOVE is ~95-105, versus ~60 at 2% yields in 2017-19. So 105 is roughly \"rates stay here and nothing calms down\", not \"a decade of crisis\". But the window must START from ~70-90 (2025 close reported at 63.96, 2024 ~100-110). Two-phase build: 2027-2031 ~105 (fiscal/AI-capex/inflation-impulse phase, duration supply against dealer balance sheets, repression-vs-spiral belief dispersion), 2032-2036 ~90 (post-bust disinflation phase in my own CQ2 path). 10-yr average = (5 x 105 + 5 x 90)/10 = 97.5. To clear 105 the back half must stay stressed at ~105+ as well, i.e. fiscal dominance persisting through the digestion phase. With sd ~12 on the decade average: P = 1 - Phi((105-97.5)/12) = 1 - Phi(0.625) = 0.266; lifted to 0.36 for the bp-normalization tailwind if nominals sit at 4.5-5%, then cut 0.02 for ICE methodology-change/discontinuation annul risk, which is one-way against a clean YES. P(A) = 0.34.\nCONJUNCT B (an MSCI World >= 25% peak-to-trough drawdown in which G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominal fails to fall >= 50bp, or rises >= 25bp). Note the OR adds nothing: \"rises >= 25bp\" is a strict subset of \"fails to fall >= 50bp\", so the operative test is only that yields do not rally 50bp — anything from -49bp upward qualifies, which is far looser than the \"stocks down AND yields up\" scan most forecasters run. Step 1